HTML (Beginner → Intermediate → Advanced)

## 🟢 BEGINNER LEVEL

### 🔴 HTML kya hai
**What is it?** HTML (HyperText Markup Language) webpage ka structure/skeleton banata hai — tags ke through content ko define karta hai.
**Why used?** Bina HTML ke browser ko pata nahi chalega ki heading kaha hai, paragraph kaha hai, image kaha hai.
**Syntax**
```html
<tagname>content</tagname>
```
**Example**
```html
<h1>Hello World</h1>
```
**Practice:** Ek blank .html file banao aur "Hello World" heading print karo.

### 🔴 Basic HTML Structure
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Page Title</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Content yaha aata hai</h1>
</body>
</html>
```
**Important Points**
- `<!DOCTYPE html>` browser ko batata hai ye HTML5 document hai
- `<html>` root element hai
- `<head>` me meta info hoti hai (page pe nahi dikhti)
- `<body>` me visible content hota hai

### 🔴 Tags, Elements, Attributes
- **Tag** → `<p>` (markup)
- **Element** → `<p>Text</p>` (opening tag + content + closing tag)
- **Attribute** → extra info tag ke andar: `<img src="pic.jpg" alt="photo">`

**Common Mistake:** Closing tag bhoolna (`<p>` likha but `</p>` nahi likha)

### 🟡 Comments
```html
<!-- Ye comment hai, browser me nahi dikhega -->
```

### 🔴 Headings & Paragraph
```html
<h1>Biggest heading</h1>
<h6>Smallest heading</h6>
<p>Paragraph text</p>
```
**Important:** Sirf ek `<h1>` per page use karo (SEO ke liye best practice)

### 🟡 Formatting Tags
`<b>` bold, `<strong>` important bold, `<i>` italic, `<em>` emphasized italic, `<br>` line break, `<hr>` horizontal line

### 🔴 Links
```html
<a href="https://google.com" target="_blank">Visit Google</a>
```
`target="_blank"` new tab me open karta hai.

### 🔴 Images
```html
<img src="photo.jpg" alt="description" width="300">
```
`alt` accessibility aur SEO ke liye zaroori hai — image na load ho to text dikhta hai.

### 🔴 Lists
```html
<ul>
  <li>Unordered item</li>
</ul>
<ol>
  <li>Ordered item</li>
</ol>
```

### 🟡 Tables
```html
<table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Age</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Rahul</td><td>21</td></tr>
</table>
```

**Practice (Beginner)**
1. Apna intro page banao (heading + paragraph + image)
2. 5 links ki list banao
3. Ek simple table banao (3 rows, 3 columns)

