## 🟡 INTERMEDIATE LEVEL

### 🔴 Forms
```html
<form action="/submit" method="POST">
  <label for="name">Name:</label>
  <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required>
  <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>
```
**Important Points**
- `action` → kaha data jayega
- `method` → GET (URL me data) ya POST (body me data)
- `name` attribute zaroori hai warna form data submit nahi hoga

### 🔴 Input Types
`text`, `email`, `password`, `number`, `date`, `checkbox`, `radio`, `file`, `range`, `color`, `submit`

```html
<input type="email" placeholder="Enter email">
<input type="checkbox" checked> Remember me
<input type="radio" name="gender" value="male"> Male
```

### 🔴 Labels
```html
<label for="email">Email</label>
<input type="email" id="email">
```
`for` aur `id` match hone chahiye — accessibility ke liye important.

### 🟡 Buttons, Select/Option, Textarea
```html
<select name="city">
  <option value="jaipur">Jaipur</option>
  <option value="delhi">Delhi</option>
</select>
<textarea rows="4" cols="30"></textarea>
<button type="button">Click Me</button>
```

### 🔴 Form Validation Attributes
`required`, `minlength`, `maxlength`, `pattern`, `min`, `max`

```html
<input type="text" required minlength="3" maxlength="10">
```
**Common Mistake:** Sirf HTML validation pe depend hona — backend validation bhi zaroori hai (frontend validation bypass ho sakti hai).

### 🔴 Semantic HTML
**What is it?** Tags jo apna meaning batate hain (structure + meaning dono).
**Why used?** SEO better hota hai, accessibility better hoti hai, code readable hota hai.

```html
<header>Site header</header>
<nav>Navigation links</nav>
<main>
  <section>
    <article>Blog post</article>
  </section>
  <aside>Sidebar</aside>
</main>
<footer>Footer content</footer>
```

| Tag | Use |
|---|---|
| `header` | top section (logo, nav) |
| `nav` | navigation links |
| `main` | page ka main content (ek hi baar use) |
| `section` | related content ka group |
| `article` | independent content (blog, news) |
| `aside` | sidebar/related info |
| `footer` | bottom section |

### 🟡 figure/figcaption
```html
<figure>
  <img src="chart.png" alt="Sales chart">
  <figcaption>Fig 1: Monthly Sales</figcaption>
</figure>
```

### 🟡 audio/video
```html
<video src="movie.mp4" controls width="400"></video>
<audio src="song.mp3" controls></audio>
```

### 🟡 iframe
```html
<iframe src="https://example.com" width="600" height="400"></iframe>
```
Kisi doosri website/content ko embed karne ke liye (YouTube video, Google Maps).

### 🟡 details/summary
```html
<details>
  <summary>Click to expand</summary>
  <p>Hidden content dikhta hai click karne pe</p>
</details>
```

### 🟡 Data Attributes
```html
<div data-user-id="42" data-role="admin">User</div>
```
Custom data store karne ke liye, JS se `element.dataset.userId` se access hota hai.

**Practice (Intermediate)**
1. Login form banao (email, password, remember me checkbox)
2. Registration form banao with validation
3. Ek blog page semantic HTML se structure karo (header, nav, article, footer)

